## Count number of digits in each password

You can count the number of digits in each password using the function `count_matches` like this:

::: {#5eee6fda .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .with_columns(pl.col('Password').str.count_matches(r'\d')
               .alias('Num_of_Digits'))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Password</th><th>Num_of_Digits</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>u32</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;marm1te&quot;</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;jam543&quot;</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;p3anutButt3r&quot;</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
